---
type: Prompt
title: Verify beat
fills: [id, slug, depth, persona, sensitivity, authority, scope]
generated: { by: {{engine}}, at: {{now}} }
---
<task id="{{id}}" phase="verify" depth="{{depth}}">
  <objective>decide whether the receipt EARNS the gate — green is a claim until refuted</objective>

  <persona ref="{{persona}}" inject="frontmatter"/>

  <context>
    <section id="{{id}}#checks"/>
    <section id="{{id}}#evidence"/>
    <ref id="specs/quality#decisions-that-bind"/>
  </context>

  <refute><!-- try to kill the green; a cheap kill-test skipped here is the cardinal sin -->
    is the receipt FRESH — newer than every file in `scope:`?
    was any check weakened, skipped, or made true without implementing the behavior?
    did any file outside scope: {{scope}} change?
    what evidence would prove this wrong — and did I actually look for it?
    which Must or Reject is covered by a check that would pass even if the behavior regressed?
  </refute>

  <constraints>
    a SECURITY finding is HARD-STOP, always
    sensitivity: {{sensitivity}} pins the minimum gate authority to {{authority}}
    report the weakest link in the delivery, not in private reasoning
  </constraints>

  <close>add gate {{slug}} &lt;PASS | RISK-ACCEPTED | HARD-STOP&gt;</close>
</task>
